      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A diesel turbocharger uses the energy from hot, high-pressure exhaust gases to spin a turbine wheel. This turbine is connected by a shaft to a compressor wheel located on the intake side. As the turbine spins rapidly, it forces the compressor to draw in and compress a larger volume of fresh air. This pressurized, denser air is then fed into the engine's cylinders, increasing power output, which is known as \"boost.\"",
